# Prisma computes each migration's checksum against its committed bytes,
# then verifies it again on every `migrate dev`/`migrate deploy` run. With
# no rule here, Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true) silently convert
# these files to CRLF, which changes that checksum without changing
# anything git itself reports as a diff -- "migration modified after
# applied" false positives that block every future migration from a
# Windows machine once the drift compounds. Migration files are also never
# meant to be edited by hand after being applied, so forcing LF here is
# free: nothing legitimately needs CRLF in a generated migration.sql.
prisma/migrations/**/*.sql text eol=lf
